# Desktop application identity

## Identity

- **LazyCodingAgent** is a **native LCL desktop application** (Windows, Linux, macOS).
- It is intentionally **not** modeled as a single-page Electron app, embedded web shell, or in-app “settings SPA.”
- Treat it as **professional desktop software**: predictable windowing, menus, and focused dialogs—not a browser tab with a sidebar.

## Classic professional patterns (preferred)

- **Main window:** persistent shell with navigation, docked panels, utility areas, and status bar ([`mainunit.lfm`](mainunit.lfm)).
- **Focused work in forms:** settings and secondary tasks open as **designer-owned `TForm` + `.lfm`** pairs—e.g. [`frmSettings.pas`](frmSettings.pas), [`frmNewWorkspace.pas`](frmNewWorkspace.pas), [`frmWorkspaceRules.pas`](frmWorkspaceRules.pas), [`frmHelp.pas`](frmHelp.pas)—shown from the menu or existing entry points, not crammed into one scrollable panel in the main view.
- **Menus and shortcuts** for commands; **dialogs** for confirm, edit, and short wizard flows.
- **Multi-surface desktop behavior** is normal: detachable panels ([`uPanelDetach.pas`](uPanelDetach.pas)), modal dialogs, and separate forms where that fits the task.

## Modern design (not retro chrome)

- Visual polish comes from the **LCA Design System** and **LcaTheme** (dark/light, themed controls, tab bars, markdown views)—see [`lazarus-visual-designer.mdc`](lazarus-visual-designer.mdc).
- **“Old school”** here means **structure and interaction model** (forms, menus, docking, native widgets)—not unstyled or legacy-looking UI.

## Do / don’t for agents

**Do:**

- Add or extend **`frm*.pas` / `.lfm`** for new settings or focused user flows.
- Wire new UI from the **main menu**, toolbar, or established entry points.
- Keep geometry and hierarchy in the **Form Designer** (`.lfm`); follow layout rules in [`lazarus-lcl-layout.mdc`](lazarus-lcl-layout.mdc).

**Don’t:**

- Default to one full-window “settings page,” client-side **routes**, or SPA-style navigation inside the main content unless the user explicitly asks.
- Use Electron-only metaphors (hamburger-only nav, everything inline in a single surface) as the primary pattern.
- Replace **form-based** app configuration with a single embedded browser page for settings.

## Related rules

- **Implementation:** [`lazarus-visual-designer.mdc`](lazarus-visual-designer.mdc) — `.lfm`, LCA components, theming.
- **User-visible changes:** [`user-help.mdc`](user-help.mdc) — update in-app User Guide when behavior changes.
